# Downloaded documents. The index that records every URL and its sha256
# is tracked; the bytes themselves are not, because they run to gigabytes
# and the register is the authoritative copy. tools/fetch_all.py refills
# this from the index.
cache/blobs/
cache/.last-request
logs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
cache/.fetch-lock

# Per-run reports from the build and the two checks. report.py reads all
# three to write REPRODUCE.md, which is the tracked record of what they
# measured. The build and verify reports carry a wall-clock built_at and
# an elapsed time, so tracking them would make two otherwise identical
# builds differ; the completeness report carries neither, but it is the
# same kind of thing and tracking it alone would leave the tree dirty
# after every run.
build-report.json
verify-report.json
completeness-report.json
